    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36914" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pō^lydămas</span></b>  (the o
		made long by the requirements of the verse), antis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πολυδάμας</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Trojan</i>, <i>son of Panthous and
				friend of Hector</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12, 547</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 5,
			94</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pō^lydămantēus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Polydamas</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					12, 212</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A famous athlete</i>, <i><span class="en">Val. Max.
				9, 12, 10</span></i>
			<i>ext.</i></div>
